        "titolo_orig": "'Atmosphere closer to wartime': Moscow’s muted Victory Day reflects growing security fears",
        "testo_it": "La parata per la vittoria a Mosca riflette il clima di insicurezza e tensione bellica in Russia.",
        "priorita": "Alta",
        "id_gruppo": 3,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260509-gr%C3%A9goire-roos",
        "orario": "15:22",
        "timestamp": 1778332964,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Atmosphere closer to wartime': Moscow’s muted Victory Day reflects growing security fears Europe Issued on: 09/05/2026 - 15:22 Modified: 09/05/2026 - 15:26 Russia’s scaled-down Victory Day celebrations highlighted mounting security concerns and the strain of the war in Ukraine, according to Chatham House analyst Grégoire Roos. Speaking to FRANCE 24, Roos said tighter security, internet shutdowns and fears of Ukrainian drone strikes created an atmosphere “closer to wartime protection” than national triumph, even as President Vladimir Putin continues to retain broad public support. 'Clean break' with Orban: Hungary's Magyar to usher in 'new era' 09/05/2026 Europe Magyar to succeed Orban as Hungary's new prime minister 09/05/2026 Europe Hungary’s Magyar set to be sworn in as new prime minister 09/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus-hit cruise ship heads for Canary Islands to evacuate passengers 09/05/2026 Europe Russia marks Victory Day with scaled-back parade 09/05/2026 Europe UK: The end of the traditional two-party system? Starmer faces crushing defeat in local polls 08/05/2026 Europe Substantial win for Nigel Farage's Reform UK in local elections 08/05/2026 Europe Energy security vs climate crisis: Norway reopens three old gas fields 08/05/2026 Europe Keir Starmer's Labour braces for heavy losses in UK local elections 08/05/2026 Europe"
